caption: Numerical Mastery

Word — Tier 2 or Tier 3: no separate 100/300-point investment floor applies. Every Word, element, or equivalent purchasable syntactic skill in the Tradition's complete Mastery lexicon must be at effective 16+ at Tier 2 or effective 20+ at Tier 3, unless the explicit skill-cap exception in Section 5.6 requires the lower effective cap. A Word that is not represented by a skill does not acquire a new skill solely from this rule; use the actual Word or category skill structure and any required Word purchases defined by the Tradition. If the Tradition also uses a distinct central or governing casting skill, that skill is effective 20+ at Tier 2 or 30+ at Tier 3. The explicit skill-cap exception in Section 5.6 applies when the Tradition's required governing traits impose a lower written ceiling. Magery or Power Investiture is 3 at Tier 2 or 6 at Tier 3 where relevant; other governing traits use the normal Tier standard. Preserve grammar, authorship, consequential-use, and other local requirements.
